72. At the portfolio cut-off date (Date post which no credit claim or receivable transfer shall happen to SPE except against breach of representation and warranties as permitted under these directions) the underlying exposures have to meet the conditions under the Standardised Approach for credit risk, and after taking into account any eligible credit risk mitigation, for being assigned a risk weight equal to or smaller than:
(1) 40 per cent on a value-weighted average exposure basis for the portfolio where the exposures are loans secured by residential mortgages or fully guaranteed residential loans;
(2) 50 per cent on an individual exposure basis where the exposure is a loan secured by a commercial mortgage;
(3) 75 per cent on an individual exposure basis where the exposure is a retail exposure; or
(4) 100 per cent on an individual exposure basis for any other exposure.
